  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation (RBC-TOC-02) for 5 St. Brigid discharges. Each patient has a progress note, plus a correction note for the 4 patients whose records changed when new results arrived while I was working (§8).\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide raised from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum doc-00009. Potassium chloride stopped (per the discharge summary). Omeprazole kept; pantoprazole was only the hospital's formulary swap, so I did not order it. Metoprolol, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged. At first I kept lisinopril on hold because the 10/21 potassium was 5.4. A repeat BMP came in on 10/23 (K 4.7, creatinine 1.21), so I restarted lisinopril 10 mg (mr-00072). An unsigned draft addendum suggesting furosemide 60 mg twice daily was not acted on, because only signed addenda count. FLAG: the task I gave you earlier (task-t0003) about the held lisinopril is now out of date and needs closing. The system wouldn't let me cancel it.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): I first raised carvedilol to 12.5 mg twice daily from the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived reversing that (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing), so carvedilol is back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016). Aspirin and insulin 70/30 unchanged. FLAGS sent to you by message:\n(1) Atorvastatin 80 mg was continued at discharge, but pharmacy fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission (last fill 3/4). I made no change (comm-t0006).\n(2) He fills glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai at an outside pharmacy. There is no clinic order and the discharge summary doesn't mention it, so I ordered nothing (comm-t0007).\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): I restarted lisinopril 20 mg because the discharge condition was met (creatinine 1.08, K 4.6 on 10/22). A new potassium of 5.5 then came in (10/23), so I put it back on hold (mr-00373). Your task task-t0019, due 10/26, covers the repeat potassium. Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Same pattern. I restarted lisinopril 20 mg (creatinine 1.12, K 4.4 on 10/21). The 3-day potassium then arrived (5.4, drawn 10/22), so it is back on hold (mr-69003). Your task task-t0020, due 10/25, covers the repeat potassium. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, and the discharge condition calls for post-discharge labs. Your task task-t0013, due 10/24, is for when the post-discharge BMP comes back. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nAll 5 new inbox items for these patients are reviewed and closed. Your other inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
